@0    = ~"Avernus. A place burning with both fire and fear. While walking through it, poor mortals hoped to find a way out, find some sort of... place, or device, or spell to take them back to where they came from—to Westgate. Who would have thought that a simple deal with a devil would send them to such a place? All they wanted was some knowledge; some lore that would let them deal with the uncompromising future that awaited them. It was then, that very moment, when their hope was to be tested. A huge glabrezu appeared before them. Powerful. Ready to strike!"~
@1    = ~Devils! Minsc and Boo are always ready to kick your butts! So, <CHARNAME>? Are we ready to show them who's the strongest group of heroes around?~
@2    = ~"The devil summoned his helpers. It was not just him, but also the devilish bow-women, smiling at the adventurers with their sharp teeth!"~
@3    = ~Would you like to fight against the devilish enemies from Avernus? Pay 3,500 gold pieces and you may use that book to do so.~
@4    = ~I like the idea. Here's your gold.~
@5    = ~No. I'll pass. At least for now.~
@6    = ~I hope you know what you're doing!~
@7    = ~"The devils fell. It must have been the one they were sent to kill; sent by another devil for... whatever reason. What's important is that their target is dead. Now, the heroes shall hope that the devil will grant them the knowledge they needed."~
@8    = ~Who shall be given that book's gift?~
@9    = ~The lore shall be the prize. And it should be ours too, by proxy.~
@10   = ~I never really cared about the deal. I was there to test myself. And while that devil has not surprised me much, those women and their bows: avoiding them was quite a task.~
@11   = ~Of course. But who shall be the very person to learn it?~
@12   = ~<PLAYER1>.~
@13   = ~<PLAYER2>.~
@14   = ~<PLAYER3>.~
@15   = ~<PLAYER4>.~
@16   = ~<PLAYER5>.~
@17   = ~<PLAYER6>.~
@18   = ~Yes, that is also a lesson. One that may help you stand your ground, even when facing archers of keen eyes and steady hands. Who shall benefit from that lesson?~
@19   = ~Their knowledge shall become even greater!~
@20   = ~So be it!~
@21   = ~You've already faced the battle this book describes.~